    LICENSES/Commons-Clause.txt

The Commons Clause modifies the Apache License grant so that the license does
not grant the right to Sell the Software, as "Sell" is defined in that
condition. This restriction applies to Boardwright itself and Boardwright-
derived tooling/template distributions. It is not intended to restrict normal
use of Boardwright to create hardware projects.

Boardwright Hardware Output Exception
-------------------------------------

Using Boardwright to create, edit, build, preview, manufacture, document, or
release a hardware project does not impose the Boardwright license on the
user's hardware design, project files, manufacturing outputs, release
artifacts, or project-specific documentation, except for Boardwright template
material copied into those outputs.

Downstream hardware projects may be licensed by their owners under licenses of
their choice, subject to any third-party material they include and any copied
Boardwright template material or notices that must be preserved.

